+# auto_kernel X12 overlay (2026-09-21): AK_X12_ROPE=1 routes the fused QKV rotary embedding --
+# forward and backward, the training call (sbhd, not interleaved, cp_size 1, no start positions,
+# bf16) -- to the Triton module at AK_X12_KERNEL_DIR/fused_qkv_rope.py (the rope_qkv task's
+# winner: libdevice cos/sin, TE's fma order, exact negation; byte-identical to
+# tex.fused_qkv_rope_forward / _backward on the task's nine cases).  Any other call keeps TE's
+# kernels.  Rank 0 prints one ARMED line at the first forward.
+# (Llama 3.1 8B campaign, 2026-10-02: TE 2.20.0+131157b5's rope.py is byte-identical to TE 2.19's, so these hunks apply
+#  unchanged; a first-call byte check against TE's kernels was added below.)
+# (sec 168: ported to the 20260929 image -- rope.py is identical there (sha 86d7e3f8), so the hunks are
+# unchanged; mcore 0.20 attention.py:1609 still calls apply_fused_qkv_rotary_pos_emb with the defaults
+# above, and FP8 attention (fp8_dpa, not fp8_mha) leaves q/k/v and dq/dk/dv in bf16 around this op.)
